# IdeaHunt Project Rules

## Language

- Pure JavaScript only — NO TypeScript, NO .ts/.tsx files
- All files use .js or .jsx extensions

## Framework

- Next.js 15 App Router
- API routes in `app/api/*/route.js`
- Pages in `app/page.jsx`
- No `use server` unless absolutely needed

## UI

- shadcn components from `@/components/ui/`
- Tailwind CSS v4 for all styling
- No inline styles, no CSS modules
- Icons via lucide-react only

## Data Fetching

- No database — all data fetched live from RSS/APIs
- Caching via Next.js `export const revalidate = 21600` (6hrs)
- All fetching happens in `lib/rss-fetcher.js`

## Sources (5 total, no more for MVP)

- r/SomebodyMakeThis — Reddit JSON API, 1+ intent signals
- r/AppIdeas — Reddit JSON API, 2+ intent signals
- r/Entrepreneur — Reddit JSON API, 3+ intent signals
- Hacker News — hnrss.org RSS, 4 targeted queries
- Dev.to — REST API, #buildinpublic + #indiehackers tags, 2+ signals

## Classification

- Keyword-based only, no AI/external API
- 14 categories defined in `lib/classifier.js`
- Returns: { category, secondary[], confidence }

## File Structure

```
app/page.jsx             → dashboard
app/api/ideas/route.js   → fetch + classify
lib/sources.js           → source configs
lib/classifier.js        → keyword classifier
lib/rss-fetcher.js       → fetch + normalize
components/IdeaCard.jsx
components/IdeaModal.jsx
components/MasonryGrid.jsx
components/Filters.jsx
```

## What NOT to do

- No TypeScript
- No database (Supabase, Prisma, etc.)
- No external backend
- No trends page (Phase 2)
- No bookmarks (Phase 2)
- No user auth
